# Sovereign Prompt Implementation Plan

The objective is to imbue the Sovereign Command Center with its own "Antigravity"—a natural language interface for direct swarm interaction and intelligence retrieval.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Cognitive Layer**: The prompt bar will leverage the swarm's existing LLM infrastructure ([MultiLLMClient](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/llm.ts#105-155)), which uses zero-cost routing via local models and the Antigravity quantum channel.

## Proposed Changes

---

### [Command Center UI]

#### [MODIFY] [AdminSovereign.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/src/pages/AdminSovereign.tsx)
- **Prompt Bar**: Add a sleek, sticky prompt input area at the bottom of the log stream.
- **AI Chat Module**: Implement a separate toggle or persistent panel for AI conversations.
- **Micro-animations**: Add "thinking" state animations and message streaming visuals.

---

### [SCC Server Backend]

#### [MODIFY] [scc_server.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/scripts/scc_server.ts)
- **Prompt Receiver**: Listen for `prompt` events from the UI.
- **Intelligence Bridge**: Initialize the [MultiLLMClient](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/llm.ts#105-155) and route user queries.
- **Stream Relay**: Emit `ai_response` chunks or completed messages back to the dashboard.

#### [NEW] [prompt_handler.ts](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/scripts/prompt_handler.ts)
A dedicated module to:
- Contextualize user prompts with swarm status and mission data.
- Manage message history for stateful conversations.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `npx tsx scripts/test_prompt.ts`: Verify that a test prompt receives a coherent response from the [MultiLLMClient](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/llm.ts#105-155).

### Manual Verification
- Type "What is the current swarm status?" into the new prompt bar and verify the AI response correctly reflects telemetry data.
- Verify that messages scroll naturally and the "thinking" indicator works as expected.
